        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Hence, for the fixed point  $ z_* $ the condition of Proposition 3 is satisfied. Therefore, except for a set of parameters  $ \\kappa \\in D $ of zero measure, the nondegeneracy condition of Assumption 2 holds on any band  $ K_\\kappa $ for which  $ z_*\\in K_\\kappa $. In this case, by Theorem 4, for almost all initial conditions  $ z_0\\in K_\\kappa $ the trajectory of the real model does not stick on average to any affine hyperplane in  $ \\mathbb{R}^6 $ and is affinely integrally exciting.",
            "block_bbox": [
